  "ties_disclosure": {
    "reason": "The taps are drawn and expressible (sky130 tap 65/44 is a dedicated tap layer; n-wells are drawn on nwell 64/20), but klt erc's ties[].well_layer checks every merged shape on that one layer against a single declared net, and this block's nwell layer holds two differently-biased well classes: four PMOS-body wells strapped to VDD and two vertical-PNP base wells strapped to VSS. No well-side narrowing key exists (tap_requires/tap_is_dedicated/tap_boxes narrow the tap; well_boxes is rejected alongside a drawn well_layer), so either declaration reports the other class as a false erc.missing_tie. Reproduced in this directory as erc-nwell-tie-spec.known-gap.vdd.json and .vss.json; filed upstream as 2AMLogic/klayout-tools#2339. Cleared by a klt build with a well-side selector, not by a redrawn layout.",
    "kind": "tool_limitation"
  },
